WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.650
Spread your ebony wings,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.120
and strike the ground with the speed of lightning!

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
Synchro Summon!

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.100
Rain down, Assault Blackwing — 
Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.080
No one here in B-block's seen the suspects, either.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.560
Well, that's the best I can do.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.190
Don't go out!

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.920
They'll find you.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.850
This is your hometown?

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.570
Yeah. Though I don't know where I was 
born or what my parents look like.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.130
I'm the same way.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.780
I don't know what my mom looks like, either.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.990
The security guys are here, too.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.950
The slums belong to us, the Commons...

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.400
This is no time to be separating Tops from Commons!

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.930
Academia will eventually try to unite the dimensions.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.040
There's no telling when they'll try to 
attack the Synchro Dimension, too.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.630
I'm looking for a man named Yuya Sakaki!

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.960
Do you know anything?

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.550
Communications are also being disrupted.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.840
Restrictions in this dimension seem awfully strict...

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.580
Hey, Dennis! Why don't you join me?

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.160
Right, right.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.080
But the sun's so bright...

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.020
Wow!

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.490
That's magic, isn't it? You're good!

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.540
Why, thank you!

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.100
See you!

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.570
D-Wheels.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.750
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.430
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.850
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.060
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:57.420
The Black Whirlwind, Crow Hogan

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.160
You're amazing!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.400
You were protecting that kid, even in 
the face of all that security.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.570
No one who'd protect a child can be bad.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.100
I can tell you're a good guy.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.300
Um, who are you?

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.270
Crow, welcome back!

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:24.080
Hey, Amanda! Where are Frank and Tanner?

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.680
They went into town.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.890
They said they wanted to
help you out for once, Crow.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:29.990
What the heck?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.690
I got something good today!

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:39.720
It's tuna! I'll make tuna sandwiches!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.370
You're hungry, aren't you?

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.660
Let's eat together!

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.040
I've never seen you guys around. 
Where did you come from?

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.360
The truth is—

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.210
You really saved us before!

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.780
That was some welcome they gave us.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.710
After we came all the way from another dimension!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.450
Another dimension?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:06.270
Yeah, I'm Shingo Sawatari.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:09.340
In Maiami City, I'm known as 
the undefeated duelist.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.030
Over there is my apprentice, Yuya Sakaki.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:12.660
Hey!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.880
And this strong-willed woman is Serena.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.630
She came from a different dimension than ours.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.470
Hey, now. Did I bite off more than 
I could chew with you guys?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.470
No, it's true. We're searching for our 
teammates in this dimension.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.510
Whatever... I don't really get it,

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.010
but if you just got here, you must not 
have a place to stay, right?

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.300
You can stay here until the heat dies down.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.850
Make yourselves at home.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.550
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.520
It's show time!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.020
One, two, three!

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.440
Cool!

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.800
Forget it. Let's go, Tanner.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.570
This is nonsense!

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.710
We didn't come here for this.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.200
But, Gonny...

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.310
G-Gonny?

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:11.020
If we attract lots of attention, 
Yuya and the others will find us.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.250
Are you sure about that?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:16.990
It's fine, it's fine. Take it easy!

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.430
This is something everyone in 
City needs to know about!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.530
The dimensional war has already started!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.950
What a weirdo.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.900
Academia has already attacked the Xyz Dimension.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.900
You think we should report her?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.870
I think they might eventually attack City! 
Please listen!

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.610
Please!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.480
Trust me!

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:39.540
If we're attacked, you'll all be 
turned into cards, like this!

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.500
I know it won't be easy,

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.220
but all I can do is try to convince them.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.440
Hey, I'm sure you don't believe her, but it's true.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.690
I've also been fighting, traveling through dimensions.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.790
Then, show us! Travel between dimensions!

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.920
Oh, dear! Don't humor him!

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.770
Fine, I will!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.400
I'll travel dimensions right now, so just watch me!

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.110
Hugo, are you sure?

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.730
There's a lot of noise over there.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:09.920
Shut up!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.310
This is our chance.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.580
Flap your beautiful and heroic wings 
to carry me at the speed of light,

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.060
Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.020
Yeah, it's bogus.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.160
It's true!

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.630
You two are causing a lot of trouble.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.850
Sorry, but I had to call security.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.720
Thieves!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.820
Hey! You Commons brats!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.300
Let's run!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.370
You wait, too!

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.610
Crow's gonna love this.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.110
Crow! We're back!

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.610
Hey, where have you been?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.080
Ta-dah!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.780
Where did this come from?

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:54.240
We stole it.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.900
It was so exciting...

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.860
You idiots! No one asked you to do this!

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:00.970
But...

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.730
You always do everything.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.200
What if you got thrown into prison for this?!

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.670
Prison?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.330
Yeah. You might not know it,

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.560
but two types of people live here, Tops and Commons.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:20.480
Put simply, Tops are winners, 
and we Commons are losers.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:24.080
Winners get everything, leading lives of luxury.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:27.610
Losers struggle just to get enough 
food to survive every day.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:34.490
And if you resist in any way, security will 
capture and throw you in prison.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.460
That's awful.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.300
Yeah, it's an awful world.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.170
But we still have to find a way to live.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:45.550
That's why we Commons huddle together.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.770
It's that guy from before!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.240
Huh? But I think his clothes are different.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.800
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.680
I'm trying to—

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.620
Hey, are you the two who were at the restaurant?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.720
You mean Yuya and Serena?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:00.340
Yuzu!

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:03.480
Yeah. And the man's probably Hugo!

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.760
Where are they?

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.060
Hey, what's going on?

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.790
Our friends are in this town!

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:13.200
Security's after you, right?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.770
If they catch you, they'll throw you in prison.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.900
Fine, I get it!

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.400
I'll help you search for your friends.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.610
Just wait.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.980
Crow...

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.040
Hello, City residents!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.830
This is Melissa Claire.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:42.190
In this week's "Tell Me Melissa," we introduce you 
to the rising cutting-edge trends on the street.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.990
Today, we're introducing the street performers,

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:47.600
growing popular in Central Park!

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.650
Let's give it everything again today, Gonny!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:54.540
I will not. I'd rather search for Yuya.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.600
It looks like TV reporters are here.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.880
If you're really a duelist, you have to 
maintain your entertainment spirit.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.120
We're not dueling, though.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.090
Oh, good idea! Let's duel.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.230
What?

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.440
Many children are here.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.120
We can make it like a hero show.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.060
Are you serious?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.760
I'll play the hero, and you play the villain.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.930
Why should I?!

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.600
H-Hey, Dennis!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.880
Action Field, on!

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.070
Field Spell Crossover.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.460
Don't blame me for whatever happens!

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.140
Duel!

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.600
First, Gonny, we have to transform 
you into the villain.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.220
I activate my Continuous Spell Hot Surprise.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:45.590
I Special Summon a Fire Attribute Monster, 
Level 4 or below, to your side of the field.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:51.030
I Special Summon Performage Plushfire to your field!

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.020
This is outrageous!

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.210
Good acting.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.500
Be careful, everyone! A fire 
monster is on the rampage!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.100
And when only you have monsters 
on your side of the field,

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.520
I can Special Summon Performage 
Wind Drainer from my hand!

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:13.180
Today, it seems street performers 
are offering up a duel.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.780
A fight between good and evil is 
taking place in broad daylight.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:20.190
I, Melissa Claire, will bring you every minute of it!

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:24.680
Okay... As the hero, I'll lower 
the hammer of justice on you!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.170
I activate my spell card Performance Mage Hurricane.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.640
When there's a Performage on the field,

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:36.370
I can return all spell and trap cards 
to their owner's hand.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.280
When Hot Surprise leaves the field,

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:45.580
it destroys the monster it summoned, and deals 
400 points of damage to you!

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:49.300
Curse you, fire monster! I'm putting you out right now!

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.920
The hammer of justice dealt 
400 damage to the monster!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.760
Great job! Our hero!

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.520
I'll protect the peace for everyone!

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:00.970
Nonsense.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:07.370
Naming me the villain, just so you can look good?!

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:08.840
Gonny?

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:12.460
You won't even properly search 
for Yuya and the others.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.810
You're unfit to be a member of the Lancers!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.750
Are you mad at me?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.150
Of course I am!

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:21.220
I'll get serious about this duel and make you sorry.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:25.440
Listen, everyone! That man is no hero!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:29.590
He's a bad guy who lit me on fire, 
just to make himself more popular!

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.430
What? Is that true?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.720
This man, Gongenzaka, will now 
punish the true villain!

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:39.360
Yeah! Get him!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.860
Well, as long as they're excited...

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.940
So the jig is up, is it?

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.660
As you claim, I am the true villain!

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.780
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:13:00.330
Now, give it your best shot, wretched superhero!

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.420
The true evil has just been unveiled!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.200
Now justice will rise to face it!

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.460
Don't change that channel!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.300
My turn!

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.440
Continuous Trap Mage's Fortress.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:21.820
When I have a Spellcaster-Type Monster on my 
side of the field, you cannot declare battle!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:22.510
What?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:26.650
Now, you cannot even attack.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:29.220
What will you do now, superhero?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.360
Draw!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:35.390
The superhero made an impressive draw!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.760
I send Superheavy Samurai 
Soulhorns to the graveyard,

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:44.910
to Special Summon Level 2 Tuner Monster 
Superheavy Samurai Trumpeter!

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:51.150
And I summon Level 4 Superheavy Samurai Scales!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.570
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:58.020
I can Special Summon one Superheavy 
Samurai from my graveyard!

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:02.120
Come out, Superhuman Samurai Soulhorns!

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:07.120
Level 2 Trumpeter tunes Level 4 Scales!

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:10.090
Roar, god demon...

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.560
Arrive at the raging battlefield of evil.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.400
Synchro Summon!

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:21.540
Come to the front lines, Level 6 Superheavy 
Samurai Ogre Shutendoji!

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.040
Get him, hero!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.420
Leave it to me.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.220
When I successfully Synchro Summon Shutendoji,

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.920
and I have no spell or trap cards on my field,

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:34.590
I destroy all spell and trap cards 
on your side of the field!

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:36.050
But it won't come without a cost.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:40.390
When this card is destroyed, I draw one card!

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.780
When a Superheavy Samurai Synchro 
Monster is Special Summoned,

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:51.270
I can Special Summon Superheavy 
Samurai Soulclaw from my hand!

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.540
I activate the effect of Soulhorns!

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:59.350
Once per turn, I can equip it to a 
Superheavy Samurai monster.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:03.480
Shutendoji can be treated as a Superheavy Samurai.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:07.320
And Soulclaw's monster effect activates!

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.070
Once per turn, I can equip it to 
a Superheavy Samurai,

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.790
to increase the equip monster's attack 
and defense points by 500.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.790
Superheavy Combination

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:18.250
Shutendoji can attack from defense position.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.030
Battle!

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:22.000
I attack Wind Drainer with Shutendoji!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.900
The equip effect of Soulhorns.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.580
When I have no spell or trap cards in my graveyard,

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.050
the equip monster can attack twice.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.780
I attack directly with Shutendoji!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.220
What?

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:46.600
The superhero turned things around,

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.130
doing huge damage to the enemy 
with a consecutive attack!

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:53.720
In that case, it's time for evil show time.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.200
My turn. Draw!

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:01.200
I set the Pendulum Scale of evil with

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:06.220
Scale 3 Performage Mirror Conductor 
and Scale 6 Performage Fire Dancer!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.780
I can now summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 5 simultaneously!

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:17.520
Behold, the wicked summoning method, 
Pendulum Summon!

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:19.260
Level 4 Plushfire!

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:21.760
And Level 5 Wind Drainer!

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:26.100
What? He can do that?

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.910
Summoning multiple monsters at once?

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:31.370
What an incredible summoning method.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:34.070
We've never caught this on film before!

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.040
But it's the second time.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:40.040
What a scoop! Melissa Claire is bringing it to you!

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:42.820
So Pendulum Summon can also summon 
monsters that were previously destroyed.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:44.780
But regardless...

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.290
Another new piece is on the board.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.200
Afraid, are you?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:54.040
When Pendulum Monsters are destroyed, 
they're sent to the Extra Deck.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.990
Thus, I can bring them back, again and again!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.010
Oh, no!

00:16:58.010 --> 00:16:58.960
That's against the rules!

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.500
Of course, that isn't the end yet.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.670
I activate Wind Drainer's monster effect!

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:07.020
When this card is successfully Special Summoned,

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:08.570
its level decreases by 1!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:13.540
Then, I overlay Level 4 Plushfire 
and Wind Drainer!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.150
The show must go on!

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:24.090
Sky magician, travel around the stage magnificently!

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:26.350
Xyz Summon!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:32.310
Come out, Rank 4 Performage Trapeze Magician!

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.380
Xyz?

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.080
Rank? Not "Level"?

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.870
This previously unseen summoning method

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.730
has brought out a monster with a rank, not a level!

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:48.080
There's no telling what hidden power it might have!

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:51.420
Mirror Conductor's Pendulum Effect activates!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.680
As long as long as it's set on the Pendulum Scale,

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:58.790
the original attack and defense points of a monster 
Special Summoned to your side of the field

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:01.680
become whichever of the two was originally lower!

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.060
What?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.030
And Fire Dancer's effect...

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:09.240
It gives Trapeze Magician a piercing effect!

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:10.130
What?

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.100
I also activate the effect of Trapeze Magician!

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:17.930
I use one Overlay Unit to allow 
it to attack twice this turn!

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.780
Feel the attack of evil!

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.850
Trapeze Magician, attack Shutendoji!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:30.250
A monster equipped with Soulclaw 
can't be destroyed by battle!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.090
But Fire Dancer's effect means 
you take piercing damage.

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:40.160
Are you feeling the attack of evil, superhero?

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.870
This is nothing.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.830
But battle occurs a second time!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.370
I attack Shutendoji with Trapeze 
Magician a second time!

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.760
Since it's the second time, I think you know...

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:57.050
Shutendoji isn't destroyed, but you 
take piercing damage.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.090
I end my turn.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:03.230
Fight!

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.490
Superhero!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.320
Don't lose!

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.290
Just as I'd planned...

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.070
The superhero has taken big damage.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.280
But heroes can't be broken that easily!

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.500
Can we count on a comeback?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.740
I shall meet their expectations.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.270
My turn! Draw!

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:26.940
Once per turn, I can remove Soulhorn 
from its equip monster,

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:30.410
and summon it in defense position!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.120
The Pendulum Effect of Mirror Conductor!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:38.320
The original attack and defense points of a monster 
Special Summoned to your side of the field

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:41.090
become whichever of the original two is lower!

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:45.020
The effect of Soulclaw, equipped to 
Shutendoji, is that once per turn,

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:49.400
it can be removed and Special 
Summoned in defense position!

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:53.290
Soulclaw's attack and defense points are equal,

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.370
so Mirror Conductor's Pendulum 
Effect doesn't activate.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:59.580
By removing Soulclaw and Soulhorn,

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:03.380
Shutendoji's attack and defense 
points decrease by 500.

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:08.920
But now, I summon Tuner Monster 
Superheavy Samurai Drum!

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:13.450
Level 1 Drum tunes Level 6 Shutendoji,

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:18.010
Level 2 Soulclaw, and Level 1 Soulhorn!

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:23.210
Malevolent god, along with the roar 
of a thousand blades,

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.040
appear on the field in a whirling sandstorm!

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.040
Synchro Summon!

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:34.710
Arrive on the front lines, Level 10 Superheavy 
Samurai Warlord Susanowo!

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:40.600
But Mirror Conductor's Pendulum Effect

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:45.190
makes its original attack and defense points 
whichever of the two stats is lower!

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.560
Susanowo's monster effect!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:52.910
When this card is in defense position, and I have 
no spell or trap cards in my graveyard,

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:57.300
I can pay 500 life points to use a 
spell card in your graveyard.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:03.200
I activate the spell card Performance 
Mage Hurricane in your graveyard!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:07.130
I return all spell and trap cards 
to their owner's hand!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.950
Mirror Conductor's Pendulum Effect ends,

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:14.180
and Susanowo's points go back to normal?

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.920
Susanowo can attack while in defense position.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:18.960
Battle!

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.660
Attack Trapeze Magician.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:23.380
Kusanagi Sword Slash!

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.420
Darn, I lost...

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.440
Yeah!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.040
The hero won magnificently!

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:36.030
City's peace has been protected 
by this fine young man!

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:38.140
That's all from Melissa Claire!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.920
Are you sure this method isn't a bit dishonest?

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:47.110
What are you talking about? 
Gonny, you were—

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:49.450
That was quite impressive.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.190
You are both very skilled. I like you!

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:56.160
Um, who are you?

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.970
I am the promoter, Gallagher!

00:21:58.970 --> 00:22:01.630
I was hoping to make use of your skills.

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:09.190
I'm asking if you want to fight some strong duelists...

00:23:43.250 --> 00:23:48.270
Now, we're here! This is City's greatest 
underground dueling venue.

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:51.450
We run illegal gambling duels here.

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:53.240
It's a dark gambling den!

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:57.210
Gambling duels? How could you 
bring us to a place like this?

00:23:57.210 --> 00:24:00.000
Wait, Gonny! Not that way!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.310
Is that... Kurosaki?

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:07.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Invitation to the Dark Duels.

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:09.930
The fun is only getting started!
